cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, adapt, implement, or extend this framework, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PSI Field Lab: Synthetic Calibration and Prospective Field Validation Protocol"
abstract: >-
  A two-stage, data-centered methodology for documenting, synchronizing,
  auditing, and reviewing multimodal field observations in anomalous and
  paranormal research contexts. Stage I is a synthetic calibration
  demonstration (fixed seed 333) that tests data integration, quality gates,
  transparent scoring, unsupervised anomaly detection, participant-level site
  repeatability, sensitivity analysis, constrained language-model review, and
  run-level audit packaging. Stage II is a prospective real-data field protocol
  (Muse 2 EEG, Polar RR intervals, body cameras, independent audio recorder,
  environmental instruments) with matched target and control sessions,
  blinding, preregistration, and repetition requirements. The framework is not
  designed to prove or disprove paranormal causation.
